<newsitem itemid="802317" id="root" date="1997-08-15" xml:lang="en">
<title>SINGAPORE: OUE 1997 H1 net profit falls 4.3 pct.</title>
<headline>OUE 1997 H1 net profit falls 4.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>	  (in million of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     13.60   vs   14.21</p>
<p>    Dividend(percent)		     6.00   vs    6.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    10.82   vs   11.31</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents)   9.83   vs   10.02</p>
<p>    Turnover				 81.84   vs   79.65</p>
<p>    Investment income		     5.45   vs    5.33</p>
<p>    Other income/interest income	1.21   vs    1.28</p>
<p>    Interest expense			4.16   vs    4.18</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 19.66   vs   20.54</p>
<p>    Depreciation on land &amp; buildings  2.63   vs    2.80</p>
<p>    Other depreciation		    4.29   vs    3.41</p>
<p>    Tax					 5.82   vs    6.03</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (Loss)   0.24   vs    0.31 (loss)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay			   September 12, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open		  September 1, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Hotel-based Overseas Union Enterprise Ltd, a unit of Overseas Union Bank, said a drop in hotel management fee income affected the group's pre-tax earnings, which fell 4.28 percent.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65) 870-3080; Fax (65) 776-8112</p>
